    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 13 with a lineup prioritized by speed and favorable matchup geometry. The strongest play of the day is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.37), who benefits from a high-floor matchup against Cavalli and a substantial 14% boost from a favorable platoon split; his leadoff positioning further solidifies his status as our primary engine for runs. **Caleb Durbin** (66.18) follows closely, capitalizing on a weak 5.10 xERA from the opposing arm and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery that maximizes his stolen base equity. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (65.44) and **Chase Meidroth** (62.45) are clear starts, with **Chase Meidroth** leveraging a 19% SP skill advantage and a prime leadoff spot to anchor the middle infield. While **Trea Turner** (60.86) faces a tougher matchup against Bradley, his elite speed profile remains non-negotiable in our 5x5 Roto chase, even with a minor 5% drag due to wind-in conditions.\n\nOur primary bench dilemma centered on **Dillon Dingler** (55.36) versus the remaining depth. While **Dillon Dingler** is a start today, he narrowly avoided the bench due to his dynamic platoon advantage (L) and the elite catcher efficiency boost. He edges out the idle **Colt Keith**, who remains benched due to a poor platoon split against the starting pitcher and an official non-starter status. We are maintaining a cautious approach with **Gary Sanchez** (48.02) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (48.17); both are hovering in the marginal category, with **Gary Sanchez** carrying the risk of a \"Lineup Pending\" tag against the dangerous Roki Sasaki. We will monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** throughout the day to ensure our depth remains prepared should any last-minute defensive adjustments be required. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Carson Benge** all sidelined by team off-days, our offensive ceiling is pinned to the speed-focused core led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin**.",
